# A clause set with no refutation, and the point of this fixture is that it does NOT
# come back `proven`.
#
#     mm-cli verify run symbolic --subject bench/tools/no_refutation.logic
#
# `check_symbolic` refutes by unit resolution, which is sound and incomplete: it can
# say "these two literals contradict each other", and it cannot say "this set is
# satisfiable" for anything past the unit-clause case. The verdict here is
# `inconclusive`, and the CLI exits 3 for it rather than 0 — exiting 0 would let a
# caller read "no refutation found" as "verified", which is the one dishonesty the
# module's own documentation refuses.

p(a)
q(b)
